 "notes": "All six kinds are new (moved in from J5) and sourced from Wikipedia pages fetched this session. Tofu types (silken, firm, extra-firm, smoked, fried, frozen) are in t; named forms with their own source (aseptic silken, smoked, kōya-dōfu, fermented bean curd, stinky tofu) are archetypes. Tempe bongkrèk was left out as an archetype (linked to fatal poisonings, not a retail product) but named in the tradition. Textured vegetable protein stays in J5. House Foods has a register entry but no named tofu product was confirmed on a retrieved page, so it has no model. Morningstar Farms' Grillers/Chik'n products were not confirmed and are left out; Gardein, Vivera and Boca were not sourced. Cauldron's country and founding year and Taifun's founding year were not stated on the retrieved pages. Tempeh UNESCO status: proposal submitted March 2024, pending (Antara); later reports disagree on dates, so no outcome is claimed. No independent test winners were sourced."
